From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:26:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fader::setLFO: oscillate between from and to when from is
 above to

The half range was made positive and added to aFrom to find the centre, so
an oscillation from a higher value to a lower one ran between aFrom and
aFrom + |aTo - aFrom| instead of between aTo and aFrom: oscillateVolume
from 1 to 0 went up to 2. The half range now keeps its sign, so the centre
is the midpoint and the oscillation moves toward aTo first. Oscillations
from a lower value to a higher one are unchanged.
---
 src/core/soloud_fader.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud_fader.cpp b/src/core/soloud_fader.cpp
index 79f1278..bf45ca5 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud_fader.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud_fader.cpp
@@ -53,7 +53,6 @@ namespace SoLoud
 		mTo = aTo;
 		mTime = aTime;
 		mDelta = (aTo - aFrom) / 2;
-		if (mDelta < 0) mDelta = -mDelta;
 		mStartTime = aStartTime;
 		mEndTime = (float)M_PI * 2 / mTime;
 	}
